        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:17#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.110.070 block 18",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 18,
          "component_id": "366d09ed-f74f-56c5-814f-49c7e8eeceac",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2022,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:18",
          "start": 1742
        },
        "quote": "(2) Eligible employees hired on January 1, 2011, and after, shall be eligible to receive severance pay at the rate of one week of salary for every year of service, prorated to the nearest month, but in no case less than four weeks salary and in no case more than 26 weeks’ salary.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:18#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.110.070 block 19",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 19,
          "component_id": "e7e785be-0101-5b37-adcb-61b8a96d3e82",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2150,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:19",
          "start": 2023
        },
        "quote": "(3) Severance pay shall be calculated using the employee’s regular base hourly wage and shall not include any premium payments.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:19#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.110.070 block 20",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 20,
          "component_id": "17fcf8d9-7ff2-5416-985a-b058951aa15a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2405,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:20",
          "start": 2151
        },
        "quote": "(4) The City may elect to make severance payments in equal increments on a pay period basis until such time as the employee receives all severance pay due. In such a case, the payment will amount at least to the base pay of a regular biweekly pay period.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:20#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.110.070 block 21",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 21,
          "component_id": "425a0a8f-2494-52bb-8ed7-1829b867e1dd",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2539,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:21",
          "start": 2406
        },
        "quote": "(5) Whether employees can draw both severance pay and unemployment compensation benefits will be dependent upon applicable State law.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:21#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.110.070 block 22",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 22,
          "component_id": "9b72c94c-c61c-5186-b873-9de60330fb93",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2676,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:22",
          "start": 2540
        },
        "quote": "(6) Employees who resign, retire or are terminated for cause shall not be eligible to receive severance pay. (Ord. 20206 § 21, 9-10-19.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.110.070:block:22#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
